1359
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,020
Why...

1360
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:34,150
Why did Cho-<i>san </i>have to die?

1361
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:43,490
We'll nab the guy who did in
Cho-<i>san </i>and Takei at any cost.

1362
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:49,710
Well, no matter what the circumstances are,
wouldn't it be better to work with Kambe?

1363
00:02:49,710 --> 00:02:53,080
He has everything you need, too.

1364
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:55,170
He's no longer...

1365
00:02:55,170 --> 00:02:57,380
...a police officer.

1366
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:02,050
How do you plan on going after the perp?

1367
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,350
This is Cho-<i>san</i>'s...

1368
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:15,440
If I remember right, he always had two.

1369
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:19,190
This actually works as a wiretap.

1370
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:22,280
And this one is the receiver.

1371
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,330
So this is how it works.

1372
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:30,000
That's why Cho-<i>san </i>didn't run
when that guy showed up.

1373
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:41,800
In other words, regardless of how Kambe acted,
Cho-<i>san</i>'s mind was already--

1374
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,300
Hoshino. What do you want?

1375
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:49,220
Inspector Kato, we're taking you into custody

1376
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:54,480
as a material witness to Chief Takei
and Inspector Nakamoto's murder.

1377
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,230
What?

1378
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:58,610
H-Hey, you...

1379
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:00,280
Everyone else at Modern Crimes

1380
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:03,280
should refrain from rash activities
and stand by for the time being.

1381
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:06,280
We'll hold on to the car keys for a while, too.

1382
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,700
Hold on!

1383
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:09,490
What's the meaning of this, Hoshino?

1384
00:04:09,490 --> 00:04:11,910
Where's Inspector Kambe?

1385
00:04:11,910 --> 00:04:15,420
He's also a material witness.

1386
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:19,840
It's useless to keep secrets from us
just because he's from the Kambe family.

1387
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,170
It was indeed this individual.

1388
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:27,300
With that said,
there's no video footage remaining, right?

1389
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:32,730
The system was forcibly shut down,
so unfortunately the security cameras...

1390
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:36,100
But I saw him with my own eyes.

1391
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:41,990
We were infiltrated to the system level that
only members of the Kambe family can control.

1392
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:46,240
In other words, the only one
who can do that other than you and I is...

1393
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,870
There is no way it can be Shigemaru.

1394
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:53,960
My child... 19 years ago, he...

1395
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:58,130
You've been aware?
That my father is still alive?

1396
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:00,840
Then why?

1397
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:03,630
It's only natural
for a parent to protect their child.

1398
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:08,220
Shigemaru had his own reasons.

1399
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,520
If so, don't you think it's natural for a child

1400
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:18,810
whose mother was murdered
to have a grudge against that murderer?

1401
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:35,370
I'm going after that man.

1402
00:05:35,370 --> 00:05:38,170
However, he intentionally showed his face,

1403
00:05:38,170 --> 00:05:40,460
so you should consider
the possibility of a trap.

1404
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:43,800
Besides, we cannot trust HEUSC, either.

1405
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:46,090
The moment you pick up his trail, let me know.

1406
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:49,140
However, if this is a trap,
you'll be in danger and--

1407
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:50,680
What about it?

1408
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:04,150
I'm hungry.

1409
00:06:04,150 --> 00:06:07,780
I'm going to go buy lunch,
so can I borrow the car keys?

1410
00:06:09,070 --> 00:06:10,620
Oh, Kamei.

1411
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,280
The kebab truck is nearby
next to the park, right?

1412
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:15,450
Can you go buy some for us?

1413
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:18,920
Oh, that? Got it.

1414
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,050
You over there.

1415
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,880
What is it?

1416
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:31,220
Can you hold onto this until it dries?

1417
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:35,520
It'll be ruined if it gets misaligned,
so don't let go of it, okay?

1418
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,930
I'm going to go buy some lunch, too!

1419
00:06:37,930 --> 00:06:39,100
Me, too.

1420
00:06:39,100 --> 00:06:40,650
Hey!

1421
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,270
H-Hey, wait!

1422
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:44,820
It's fine, it's all right.

1423
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:48,110
They can't do anything.
They don't even have a car.

1424
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:57,200
Saeki, where on Earth did you get this from?

1425
00:06:57,200 --> 00:07:00,000
From the General Affairs director, you know?

1426
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,090
It's no good.

1427
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:07,170
Maybe the signal from the die is weak.

1428
00:07:07,170 --> 00:07:09,880
Kamei, can you climb on top of the roof?

1429
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,340
On top?

1430
00:07:13,090 --> 00:07:15,510
My clothes are going to get dirty again.

1431
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:17,850
Don't get caught by the cops!

1432
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:20,440
You're a cop too, you know.

1433
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:25,110
Even if they don't find me,
I might get reported.

1434
00:07:25,110 --> 00:07:28,190
Kamei, please lift the antenna
as high as possible!

1435
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:30,400
That's like the one good trait you have, right?

1436
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:38,690
KEBAB

1437
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:38,690
KEBAB

1438
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:38,690
KEBAB

1439
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:36,240
And try spinning around!

1440
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,580
Mom! What's that man doing?

1441
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,120
Don't look!

1442
00:07:49,670 --> 00:07:53,050
I caught it, Kamei! I caught the signal!

1443
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:55,720
Please stay in that position!

1444
00:07:57,930 --> 00:07:59,640
Please hurry.

1445
00:08:03,690 --> 00:08:05,270
I've located him!

1446
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:15,450
The target vehicle is parked at the metered
parking lot in Utagawacho, Shibuya.

